BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:3b24ac05-765f-4b9c-824f-158dfba413b6
DTSTART:20270403T130000
DTEND:20270404T210000
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is designed for anyone interested in learning the
  history\, anatomy\, and practical use of one of the most essential tools 
 in woodworking and timber processing. You’ll build your own custom axe h
 andle and learn how to hang (fit) an axe head\, ensuring a properly balanc
 ed tool. You’ll also learn how to use a broad axe to hew round logs into
  square timbers\, a foundational skill in traditional timber framing.
SUMMARY:Axecraft: Hewing & Axe Handling
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006c4DKAQ
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:10d79c11-fc86-486e-8fd4-8b57f927bb57
DTSTART:20270410T120000
DTEND:20270411T210000
DESCRIPTION:In this course\, students will engage in intellectual play\, br
 ainstorming\, and collaboration as they plan\, design\, and make an object
  with meaning. Over the course of two days\, we will work together to help
  each other produce an object that informs\, delights\, or spurs conversat
 ion. \n\n\n\nAll skill levels are welcome\, but please note that the class
  will emphasize creative process and narrative design over technical skill
  development.
SUMMARY:Creating Sculptures with Meaning
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006abtKAA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:c45278c3-421a-4af8-b1a9-72edf7f62cc6
DTSTART:20270410T130000
DTEND:20270410T210000
DESCRIPTION:In this full day workshop\, participants will gain skills neede
 d to identify woods no matter what the sample size\, be it a board\, a log
 \, or a small sample. The class will focus on common hardwoods and softwoo
 ds of North America. Skills learned can be applied to identification of no
 n-native species as well.
SUMMARY:Wood Species Identification
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006NpxKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:a5f9f751-2f01-4b8a-9354-55c800a401b9
DTSTART:20270412T120000
DTEND:20270417T210000
DESCRIPTION:In this 6-day hands-on course\, students will learn how to lay 
 out and cut full-scribe round log timber frame joinery. Students will begi
 n with scribing\, log selection and positioning logs. Once the layout is c
 omplete\, students will use a combination of chainsaws\, axes\, adzes\, ch
 isels\, gouges\, and mallets to cut precise joinery\, culminating in the a
 ssembly and raising of a small round-log timber frame.
SUMMARY:Round Log Timber Framing
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006NrZKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:4a5a6e64-c18c-418b-a343-56a43915024a
DTSTART:20270424T120000
DTEND:20270425T210000
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of timber framing while creating a beautiful m
 ailbox for your home in this approachable\, hands-on weekend class. Studen
 ts will construct a beautiful and durable mailbox post\, ready for finishi
 ng and installation. Students will learn the fundamentals of timber framin
 g\, from reading a plan and laying out joints to cutting and assembling th
 e mailbox post.
SUMMARY:Timber Frame Mailbox
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006NtBKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:66b8a34a-aac8-4e43-8eeb-ddf0390430f5
DTSTART:20270424T130000
DTEND:20270424T210000
DESCRIPTION:Are you a landowner in southeast Michigan with a hardwood fores
 t facing the challenges of overgrowth? Join the Sam Beauford Woodworking I
 nstitute (SBWI) in partnership with Forestry Management Services INC (FMS)
  and the Michigan Department of Natural Resources (MDNR) for a one-day int
 ensive course designed to empower you to make informed decisions about you
 r valuable forest resource.
SUMMARY:Timber for Today and Tomorrow: Sustainable Forest Management for La
 ndowners
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006PVBKA2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:67d5ac38-cf83-447a-a0f9-2c8b094f797d
DTSTART:20270424T130000
DTEND:20270425T210000
DESCRIPTION:This class focuses on the techniques needed to turn a hollow ve
 ssel\, a form that requires specialized tool control and a careful approac
 h to hollowing. Students will learn the fundamentals of vessel design\, sa
 fe hollowing methods\, and various finishing techniques. By the end of the
  course\, students will have completed a hollow vessel while developing sk
 ills applicable to future projects.
SUMMARY:Turning a Hollow Vessel with Greg Gallegos
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006RTlKAM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:6ca61450-c3c2-49ec-a7c3-b5d7ab58ea0f
DTSTART:20270508T120000
DTEND:20270508T210000
DESCRIPTION:Charcuterie boards are both functional and beautiful - displayi
 ng the natural beauty of hardwoods grown and milled right here in Michigan
 . Make it a gift for a birthday\, anniversary or even Mother's Day! Perfec
 t for beginners.
SUMMARY:Make a Custom Charcuterie Board
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006PYPKA2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:7e9542ac-5638-4bce-a866-4001ed87bd58
DTSTART:20270508T140000
DTEND:20270508T190000
DESCRIPTION:We’ll get that old dusty hand plane back into action in this 
 one day workshop! We will polish\, sharpen\, and tune up the body of your 
 hand plane to get it into user ready condition.
SUMMARY:Hand Plane Restoration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006PWnKAM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:91c38b48-63dc-4ee6-a7ba-86420adcc823
DTSTART:20270509T120000
DTEND:20270509T210000
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day mastering the Shakers’ timeless method for bendin
 g thin wood into elegant oval boxes. Through live demonstrations and plent
 y of hands-on practice\, you’ll discover how heat and moisture make wood
  flexible\, then learn the precise steps for shaping\, fastening\, and fin
 ishing a matched set of three nesting boxes. No prior experience or tools 
 are required—all materials and equipment are provided.
SUMMARY:Shaker Oval Box
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006RVNKA2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:3918d852-c05b-48f1-bdc6-91d6462bd4b9
DTSTART:20270509T120000
DTEND:20270509T210000
DESCRIPTION:Following the Woodwork Career Alliance (WCA) skill standards cu
 rriculum\, you will comprehensively learn all about the most common power 
 tools\, how to safely use then and make a tool caddy to take home. Working
  with woodworking machines can be dangerous without proper training\, and 
 our course provides the essential knowledge and hands-on instruction neede
 d to operate tools safely and effectively.
SUMMARY:Woodshop Safety
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006RWzKAM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:355b2838-ceb6-437a-ba3e-b1b1e0c548ec
DTSTART:20270517T120000
DTEND:20270522T210000
DESCRIPTION:This course will give students a foundational education in timb
 er framing while they work as a group to build and complete a timber frame
  pavilion. Students will gain an understanding of the materials\, tools an
 d safety standards used in the timber framing industry.
SUMMARY:Timber Framing
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006RYbKAM
END:VEVENT
