DESCRIPTION:Intro into Woodblock Printmaking is for beginners interested in
  learning about one of the oldest art forms in human history. In this clas
 s students will learn how to carve designs into wood for the purpose of pr
 inting on paper. No experience is required and all are welcome. Please bri
 ng photo reference material to transfer to wood or create your own designs
  (on paper and no larger than 5”x7”).
SUMMARY:Intro to Woodblock Printmaking
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006RdRKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:94709e63-311e-4976-8476-fde516f518e6
DTSTART:20270606T140000
DTEND:20270606T200000
DESCRIPTION:This course is perfect if you’re curious about woodworking an
 d using tools.  You don’t need any previous experience to join— just c
 ome ready to learn and get ready to master some seriously cool skills! Wit
 h the guidance of experienced instructors\, you will use a variety of  dif
 ferent tools in our shop: the table saw\, band saw\, drills\, sanders\, ha
 nd tools and more.  SBWI instructors will ensure every student has one-on-
 one
SUMMARY:Woodworking for Teens
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006TddKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:674bbe47-1d6b-4a16-b7a3-6a2cc17c587f
DTSTART:20270607T120000
DTEND:20270611T210000
DESCRIPTION:In this course\, we will explore mid-century design as students
  build their own lounge chair. Upgrade is also available to build a matchi
 ng Mid-Century Modern Ottoman during class for an additional $200. You wil
 l build the ottoman simultaneously while building your chair.
SUMMARY:Mid Century Modern Chair
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006TlhKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:0c7ea2ad-0087-460b-b1bf-286f01ab60d8
DTSTART:20270607T120000
DTEND:20270611T210000
DESCRIPTION:Students will learn a variety of joinery\, their strengths and 
 weaknesses and how to implement them into furniture making and design. We 
 will first construct a simple box to store all of our new sample joints th
 en get right into the art and technique of wood joinery. This will be a co
 mbination of hand tool and machine joinery techniques.
SUMMARY:Hand Cut Joinery
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006UjNKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:81f95c92-04a9-4574-9c60-fbcb0075593c
DTSTART:20270612T120000
DTEND:20270613T160000
DESCRIPTION:Over the course of this 2-day comprehensive class\, we will dem
 ystify how to make dovetails completely by hand. The first day will be spe
 nt cutting dovetails and pins and the second day will be dedicated to fitt
 ing joinery and constructing your project. This class is geared toward peo
 ple who have beginner woodworking skills and want to learn more advanced t
 echniques\, but students new to the woodshop are also welcome to join!
SUMMARY:Learn Dovetail Joinery
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006UmbKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:3f3c1a5d-a0ab-4a15-b900-48ea2ac0ae3d
DTSTART:20270612T130000
DTEND:20270613T200000
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Sam Beauford Woodworking Institute to make a uni
 que band saw box. Class is intended for those with limited to moderate woo
 dworking skills. We will design a box or students may choose a template pr
 ovided in class.
SUMMARY:Band Saw Boxes
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006UkzKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:93b0b9c8-bd90-4467-bed1-9237d93d04ee
DTSTART:20270614T120000
DTEND:20270618T210000
DESCRIPTION:In this course\, students will work together to build one compl
 ex\, yet manageable\, awning for over a doorway or window using the princi
 ples of stereotomy. Students will learn to use the visuospatial part of th
 eir brain\; the group of cognitive functions which analyzes and understand
 s space to solve these complexities. Students will use mental imagery and 
 navigation to process and rotate 2D and 3D objects in their mind.
SUMMARY:Stereotomy - Double Curved Structures
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006agjKAA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:c9d073fd-d95b-44e9-b4e5-0bb5b7d9e2ee
DTSTART:20270616T120000
DTEND:20270618T210000
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will push you to rethink the way you’ve been ta
 ught and to explore new teaching theory and best practices based on the Be
 yond Hands-On model. Students will explore usable teaching tools that can 
 be modified for any classroom\, any trade\, and all types of learners. Ope
 n to any and all educators. Scholarships available from NPS Historic Prese
 rvation Training Center and Preservation Maryland’s Campaign for Histori
 c Trades.
SUMMARY:How to Teach - Trades Educator Training
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V400000047MHKAY
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:763d93a2-d01a-4454-94a2-055842b55870
DTSTART:20270619T120000
DTEND:20270620T210000
DESCRIPTION:In this hands-on workshop\, participants will construct a high-
 top patio table based on the German National Carpentry Team’s design\, i
 ncorporating a self-supporting X-brace structure. You will use practical s
 tereotomy\, known as Schiftung\, to manually draw out the design full-size
 \, ensuring accurate angles and lengths for precise layout.
SUMMARY:Stereotomical High Top Patio Table
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006af7KAA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:e121c478-80b2-4479-a833-2d11ddf0081a
DTSTART:20270621T120000
DTEND:20270625T160000
DESCRIPTION:Building your own kitchen cabinets can be a cost-effective way 
 to get custom cabinets at bargain prices. Plus it is an extremely fun and 
 rewarding pursuit. In this 5-day course\, we will teach you how to build k
 itchen cabinets with a few tools in the garage.
SUMMARY:Cabinet Making
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006UoDKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:592db7bf-8d13-45fc-a135-642d00163cf8
DTSTART:20270621T120000
DTEND:20270626T210000
DESCRIPTION:Stick chairs belong to a long tradition of vernacular furniture
 . They are functional objects made by ordinary people with a limited numbe
 r of tools from the materials they had around. Over the course of six days
 \, we will construct comb-back stick chairs that attempt to channel that s
 ame spirit\, working from a shared starting point that leaves plenty of ro
 om for personalization.
SUMMARY:Welsh Stick Chair with Grace Ambrose
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006aiLKAQ
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:a9e10d0a-30dc-4ea6-b2fa-5b55b859d609
DTSTART:20270626T130000
DTEND:20270627T210000
DESCRIPTION:Dive into the world of Mid Century Modern design with our Funky
  Footstool Workshop. In this two-day course\, you'll learn the foundationa
 l skills of woodworking and upholstery by constructing a replica of the Mi
 d Century Modern footstool designed by Victor Wilkins.
SUMMARY:Mid Century Funky Footstool
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006UrRKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:b823714b-56da-4702-944a-7433af66a6d2
DTSTART:20270627T120000
DTEND:20270627T210000
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day mastering the Shakers’ timeless method for bendin
 g thin wood into elegant oval boxes. Through live demonstrations and plent
 y of hands-on practice\, you’ll discover how heat and moisture make wood
  flexible\, then learn the precise steps for shaping\, fastening\, and fin
 ishing a matched set of three nesting boxes. No prior experience or tools 
 are required—all materials and equipment are provided.
SUMMARY:Shaker Oval Box
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006UppKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:38d9c032-8842-4b2e-9148-6b8602119a4e
DTSTART:20270628T130000
DTEND:20270630T200000
DESCRIPTION:This 3-day class will teach you the basics of weaving caned sea
 ts as well as how to re-cane an antique chair.  Students will start by can
 ning small practice frames.  On these frames\, students will become famili
 ar with the traditional 6-strand weave pattern.  There may be extra time f
 or students to learn other weave patterns as well.  After the practice can
 es are complete\, students will re-cane an antique chair\, provided by SBW
 I.
SUMMARY:Intermediate Chair Caning
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006bCzKAI
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:12e5b88a-d8e3-4461-9282-b07e4844b236
DTSTART:20270705T120000
DTEND:20270710T210000
DESCRIPTION:Build two different styles of stools in six days. The first hal
 f of the class will be dedicated to building the Windsor style Hearth Stoo
 l designed by Shea Alexander. The last half of the class we will build a p
 ost & rung style bar stool designed by Zack Fealk and weave the seat with 
 Shaker tape.  This is a hand tool-intensive class where students will prim
 arily use hand tools to shape the components of their stools.
SUMMARY:2 Cool Stools
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006Ut3KAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:ab19d02b-479e-4225-9470-2265b8a51e16
DTSTART:20270705T120000
DTEND:20270709T210000
DESCRIPTION:In this course\, we will explore mid-century design as students
  build their own lounge chair. Upgrade is also available to build a matchi
 ng Mid-Century Modern Ottoman during class for an additional $200. You wil
 l build the ottoman simultaneously while building your chair.
SUMMARY:Mid Century Modern Chair
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006adVKAQ
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:3c193eda-d95e-486c-8e2b-d1481d9ba335
DTSTART:20270710T130000
DTEND:20270711T200000
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of bowl turning as you create simple side and 
 end-grain bowls followed by a more complex lidded box.  We'll begin with l
 athe safety\, basic wood science\, and a discussion of how bowl blanks can
  be made from logs in your own backyard. We will then move into turning si
 mple side grain bowls. Day two will introduce end grain bowl techniques\, 
 focused on a lidded box project or cup. No prior turning experience necess
 ary.
SUMMARY:Intro to Bowl Turning
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006c0zKAA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:99fae635-7be0-47b5-8713-1da204f0c942
DTSTART:20270712T120000
DTEND:20270716T210000
DESCRIPTION:Whether you already own an embarrassment of hand tools and want
  an elegant and portable way to store them\, or you simply want to be read
 y when your hand tool obsession (inevitably) arrives\, you need a Dutch To
 ol Chest. Under our guidance\, you’ll learn to craft each joint\, detail
  each surface\, and apply an eye-pleasing finish (choose your own color!).
  We will work with Eastern White Pine and school-provided hardware for thi
 s project.
SUMMARY:Hand Tool Woodworking: Make a Dutch Tool Chest
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006UufKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:3f0c0c97-a7cb-42be-ba93-6e54eb604883
DTSTART:20270712T120000
DTEND:20270716T210000
DESCRIPTION:The class will begin by discussing Mid-Century Modern form and 
 characteristics that define the style. Students will learn about the key e
 lements of this design movement and its impact on the furniture industry. 
 From there\, each student will design their own unique table and build a p
 rototype. Instructors will work closely with students to help them create 
 a detailed plan for building their table.
SUMMARY:Mid Century Modern Table - Design & Build
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006VNhKAM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:4a2f15c7-1df0-44dd-8967-8ddd8448fc57
DTSTART:20270717T120000
DTEND:20270718T210000
DESCRIPTION:End grain cutting boards and butcher blocks are both strikingly
  beautiful and incredibly durable. With proper care\, these hand crafted p
 ieces can last for generations.  Use them daily in your kitchen or just le
 ave them on your counter for decoration\, they are great conversation piec
 es. No matter your skill level\, this class is for you!
SUMMARY:End Grain Butcher Block Cutting Board
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006VqjKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:abe6212f-5f3d-4c16-a1ee-5d6f33fa909a
DTSTART:20270719T120000
DTEND:20270724T210000
DESCRIPTION:Your woodworking journey starts here\, with this 6-day intensiv
 e class.  Intro to Woodworking is designed for beginners interested the fu
 ndamentals of woodworking\, focusing on machine techniques.  No prior expe
 rience is required. With a maximum of 8 students\, you'll receive personal
 ized instruction in a fully equipped machine room. By the end of this clas
 s\, you will have the ability to tackle more woodworking projects on your 
 own.
SUMMARY:Intro to Woodworking
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006VtxKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:5bb54145-3aaf-4cae-a6f6-9d0536c4c625
DTSTART:20270719T120000
DTEND:20270723T210000
DESCRIPTION:"Do not make something unless it is both necessary and useful\;
  but if it is both necessary and useful\, do not hesitate to make it beaut
 iful." Spend 5 days exploring the timeless craftsmanship of the Shakers th
 rough four classic projects. We'll begin with a set of 3 nesting oval boxe
 s\, and as the days proceed we'll vary our time between turkey wing hand b
 rooms\, a two-step dovetailed Cherry step stool\, and a painted peg rail.
SUMMARY:The Shaker Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006bRVKAY
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:b0de8009-2143-4e24-9d8b-3dbd846a356d
DTSTART:20270724T140000
DTEND:20270724T200000
DESCRIPTION:Start your upholstery journey with this beginner-friendly and p
 ractical project: reupholstering a dining chair seat. This technique can b
 e applied to many types of furniture\, such as side chairs\, bar stools\, 
 ottomans\, headboards\, and more.
SUMMARY:Upholstery Basics: Reupholster a Side Chair
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006VvZKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:491ea62e-835e-474d-8971-7a6b43982973
DTSTART:20270726T120000
DTEND:20270730T210000
DESCRIPTION:Under the expert instruction of Kimberly Winkle\, students will
  learn and practice the essential principles of woodturning.  They will al
 so dive into embellishment techniques by exploring color and surface enhan
 cements. Participants will practice both spindle and faceplate turning to 
 craft candlesticks\, a small footstool\, and more. Elements of design and 
 surface embellishment\, including painting and texturing\, will also be co
 vered.
SUMMARY:Woodturning FUNdamentals\, Color & Surface Details with Kimberly Wi
 nkle
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0Hu000000cWgcKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:f44464c2-b60f-4581-816a-2016158baeef
DTSTART:20270726T120000
DTEND:20270730T210000
DESCRIPTION:This class will guide students through the transformation of Ea
 stern White Pine boards into simple\, historically accurate window sash an
 d doors. We will also cover how to repair and restore old sashes. The clas
 s will also cover how to install a window sash\, using both traditional 19
 th-century techniques and alternative approaches suited for modern constru
 ction.
SUMMARY:Historic Windows and Doors: Construction & Repair
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006W0PKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:083e0dde-3d37-42b0-b57e-031a27aa4b86
DTSTART:20270731T120000
DTEND:20270801T210000
DESCRIPTION:Learn the fundamentals skills of woodturning and milk paint in 
 a fun\, and supportive environment to create a one-of-a-kind small stool. 
  Students will learn lathe safety\, tool selection\, design aspects\, spin
 dle and faceplate turning\, along with the use of milk paint to add color 
 and personality to their finished creations.
SUMMARY:Turned & Painted Stool with Kimberly Winkle
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0Hu000000cWghKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:620e58a8-b6d0-48af-b395-e7ded29190c4
DTSTART:20270731T120000
DTEND:20270801T210000
DESCRIPTION:This course will teach students how to split (rive) wood using 
 traditional hand tools to create the materials needed for roofing\, siding
 \, and interior lath work of a historic home or cabin. The key focus of th
 is course is riving—the art of splitting wood along the grain to create 
 durable\, weatherproof building materials. Students will gain a deep under
 standing of wood grain\, learning to read and manipulate it for optimal sp
 litting.
SUMMARY:Historic Shingling & Siding Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006bL3KAI
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:e5a584eb-07dd-4b13-bcda-1d4632740144
DTSTART:20270801T130000
DTEND:20270801T200000
DESCRIPTION:The key to using hand tools correctly is a sharp edge - learn h
 ow the masters make it look so easy.  Join master woodworker and machinist
  Bob Goppold for a one day workshop on sharpening hand planes and chisels.
  Learn several techniques to make your hand plane and chisel edge “shavi
 ng sharp”.
SUMMARY:Sharpening Chisels & Planes
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006W21KAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:cc5d75a1-164d-49e7-96f3-fcc645739fa4
DTSTART:20270910T120000
DTEND:20270912T210000
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to determine the forces and loads a traditional timbe
 r frame structure (or really any structure) will see over the course of it
 s lifetime.  We will then cover sizing of beams\, basic joinery and connec
 tion design. Students will design a basic timber frame joint\, calculate i
 ts allowable design strength\, and then fabricate it out of timber. We wil
 l “bust” them by pulling them apart using a hydraulic load frame.
SUMMARY:Introduction to Timber Frame Engineering: Design/Make/Break
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006W3dKAE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:a77f28be-7c78-466e-8d1a-18cdab8de6b2
DTSTART:20270911T120000
DTEND:20270911T210000
DESCRIPTION:Following the Woodwork Career Alliance (WCA) skill standards cu
 rriculum\, you will comprehensively learn all about the most common power 
 tools\, how to safely use then and make a tool caddy to take home. Working
  with woodworking machines can be dangerous without proper training\, and 
 our course provides the essential knowledge and hands-on instruction neede
 d to operate tools safely and effectively.
SUMMARY:Woodshop Safety
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006W5FKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:aacff856-f70b-4dc3-8474-3fe5dc75fd62
DTSTART:20270912T120000
DTEND:20270912T210000
DESCRIPTION:Cutting boards are the perfect project for people at the front 
 end of their woodworking journey. They are made from beautiful hardwoods a
 nd they will add a lot of character to anyone's kitchen.
SUMMARY:Long Grain Cutting Board
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006X9NKAU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:dde29bf9-5d0f-4f62-9517-a8393b0f6c87
DTSTART:20270918T130000
DTEND:20270919T200000
DESCRIPTION:This 2-day course will teach you the very fundamentals of turni
 ng and proper tool use.  With expert guidance\, you will learn how to safe
 ly and proficiently use a lathe while turning a variety of projects. Tool 
 sharpening\, materials selection and finishing will also be covered throug
 hout the course.
SUMMARY:Intro to Woodturning
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006XAzKAM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:de9e3f2f-825c-408e-a7e4-d7752e694114
DTSTART:20270918T130000
DTEND:20270919T210000
DESCRIPTION:Intro into Woodblock Printmaking is for beginners interested in
  learning about one of the oldest art forms in human history. In this clas
 s students will learn how to carve designs into wood for the purpose of pr
 inting on paper. No experience is required and all are welcome. Please bri
 ng photo reference material to transfer to wood or create your own designs
  (on paper and no larger than 5”x7”).
SUMMARY:Intro to Woodblock Printmaking
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006XCbKAM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:8982d8f0-ed39-4d00-88f8-2f513cb5ef90
DTSTART:20270925T120000
DTEND:20270926T210000
DESCRIPTION:End grain cutting boards and butcher blocks are both strikingly
  beautiful and incredibly durable. With proper care\, these hand crafted p
 ieces can last for generations.  Use them daily in your kitchen or just le
 ave them on your counter for decoration\, they are great conversation piec
 es. No matter your skill level\, this class is for you!
SUMMARY:End Grain Butcher Block Cutting Board
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006XEDKA2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:a9852b90-8f67-4b8f-93fb-b39e94708e58
DTSTART:20270927T120000
DTEND:20271005T210000
DESCRIPTION:The Comb Back Rocking Chair class is an advanced chairmaking cl
 ass. It’s a good opportunity to learn about riving and shaving greenwood
  along its grain\, steambending\, carving a chair seat with hand tools\, a
 ssembling a complicated chair and generally using and sharpening specific 
 chairmaking tools. Turned pieces (legs\, stretchers and arm supports) are 
 provided so you won’t be turning in this class.
SUMMARY:Comb Back Rocker with Félix Bouchet
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006bMfKAI
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:dc185e5e-14a9-43f1-ae2b-062d4a7068e7
DTSTART:20271004T120000
DTEND:20271008T210000
DESCRIPTION:Few things are more satisfying than seeing ribbons of shavings 
 effortlessly peeling off a fresh green bowl blank and watching the bowl em
 erge.  This class will focus on mastering the bowl gouge for efficiently t
 urning bowls from green wood. Students will learn how to begin with fresh 
 cut logs and process them into finished bowls. Simple surface embellishing
  techniques will be covered along with the use of milk paints.
SUMMARY:Bowl Turning - From Log to Table with Mark Gardner
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006bPtKAI
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261109T044320Z
UID:1e1c5f7a-d170-4788-bcce-f3099bb59d06
DTSTART:20271009T120000
DTEND:20271010T210000
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of timber framing while creating a beautiful m
 ailbox for your home in this approachable\, hands-on weekend class. Studen
 ts will construct a beautiful and durable mailbox post\, ready for finishi
 ng and installation. Students will learn the fundamentals of timber framin
 g\, from reading a plan and laying out joints to cutting and assembling th
 e mailbox post.
SUMMARY:Timber Frame Mailbox
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ce.sbwi.edu/s/courseoffering/0P0V40000006XHRKA2
END:VEVENT
